# Brand and app id

Two layers — do not conflate them.

| Layer | Module | When it changes |
|-------|--------|-----------------|
| **Product brand** | [`src/lib/brand.ts`](src/lib/brand.ts) | User-visible rename (name, slug, domain) |
| **App id** | [`src/lib/app-id.ts`](src/lib/app-id.ts) | Almost never — storage and share protocol |

## Rules

- **User-facing** name, slug, domain, download stems, User-Agent → import `brand` from `@/lib/brand`. Do not hardcode `bricola`, `Bricola`, or `bricola.art` in components or runtime copy.
- **Storage and protocol** (IndexedDB names, share hash prefix) → import `APP_ID`, `SHARE_HASH_PREFIX`, and helpers from `@/lib/app-id`. Do not hardcode `collage` or `cl1=`.
- `APP_ID` is generic on purpose (`collage` will appear in UI copy later). **Never sprinkle the string.** Derive DB names via `previewCacheDbName()` / `trackPreviewCacheDbName()` or `` `${APP_ID}-…` ``. To find technical uses, search for the symbol `APP_ID`, not the word collage.
- Do **not** change `app-id.ts` when the product is renamed. A rename is `brand.ts` plus user-facing prose (README, changelog intro, examples in this rule).
- Repo folder and `package.json` `"name": "music-cloud"` are the git remote, not the product. Do not “fix” them during a rebrand.
- Metaphor copy (“music cloud”, “cover art cloud”) is not the product name.
